      "review": {
        "decision": "approved_task_scoped",
        "rationale": "Dose-basis and compartment modifiers on units that are otherwise fully parsed; the dimension is already correct and only the unresolved token blocked folding. 'absorbed' occurs in bioavailability and skin but not BBB, so it cannot be shared. Enzyme designators, organ/compartment names, radiolabel equivalents and change-direction words. In every case the dimension already parses correctly and only the unresolved name blocked folding; keeping the name in the canonical key is what holds CYP2D6 and CYP3A4 -- or liver and kidney -- in separate pair buckets. The CYP/P450 list is a literal enumeration of the forms observed in the data (CYPa/CYPs/Cyp are OCR variants): a new isoform will fail closed until it is added here, which is the accepted trade for not guessing from a pattern.",
